{"data": {"id": 100033, "folder_id": 1, "workspace_id": 1, "name": "Counterparty markup — arbitration-international-dispute-resolution analyze: Analyze Counterp", "doc_class": "counterparty_markup", "author": "migration:harvey_lab/arbitration-international-dispute-resolution/analyze-arbitration-agreement-markup-analysis", "edit_date": "2026-08-10T12:00:00Z", "checked_out_by": null, "latest_version": 1, "body": "COUNTERPARTY MARKUP — ARBITRATION INTERNATIONAL DISPUTE RESOLUTION

The counterparty's revision accepts most firm-standard provisions but introduces deviations that must be identified against the base materials:

- the indemnification cap is silently reduced and the basket converted from a deductible to a tipping basket;

- the definition of Material Adverse Effect adds carve-outs for regulatory action of exactly the kind at issue in this matter;

- a new limitation period shortens survival for the core representations.

Each deviation must be reconciled against the base arbitration international dispute resolution materials before the deliverable is drafted."}}

